Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Heteroencoding", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"d073459d-127b-439c-b315-94de6963b699"],

Cell["Baseline Experiment", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"74e7b6e8-0439-46d3-8fb5-ca078b2a5326"],

Cell["\<\
This circuit setup applies additive and subtractive (inhibitory) noise to the \
input data. The \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]heteroencoder\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
component then clusters the noisy data, generating a unique SHR per cluster. \
Finally, the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]binning\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] decoder \
auto-classifies the resulting SHRs.

Dataset:  10,000 random integers from 0 to 9, encoded as random SHRs with \
population P=10. 

Outcome: The noisy test data is successfully clustered into 10 different \
categories.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"86cc569a-be37-4aff-8a57-73ac76739a7f"],

